{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775232440,"nonce":"CC4gG2u7Q3TjsmoZEr0qILmLT8A=","title":"Nightshift session history is deleted on accept/reject/cleanup. Archive it for future analysis.","message":"Session dirs (.nightshift/sessions/\u003cid\u003e/) contain conversation.jsonl, raw-output.log, and state.json — all deleted by cleanup. Loses provenance data.\n\n\nMove session files to .nightshift/archive/\u003csession-id\u003e/ before deleting the session dir.\n\n- tests/test_session_utils_host.py::test_cleanup_archives_conversation\n  Assert: after cleanup, conversation.jsonl exists in .nightshift/archive/\u003csession-id\u003e/\n- tests/test_session_utils_host.py::test_cleanup_archives_state\n  Assert: after cleanup, state.json exists in archive\n- tests/test_session_utils_host.py::test_accept_archives_before_cleanup\n  Assert: after accept, archive dir contains session data\n\n- host/session_utils.py (modify — archive session data before cleanup)\n- host/constants.py (modify — ARCHIVE_DIR constant)\n\n1. Add ARCHIVE_DIR = \"archive\" to host/constants.py\n2. In host/session_utils.py cleanup function, before deleting session dir:\n   - Create .nightshift/archive/\u003csession-id\u003e/\n   - Copy conversation.jsonl, state.json, raw-output.log to archive\n3. Existing cleanup logic continues unchanged after archiving\n\nSee host/session_utils.py for existing cleanup logic.\n\nREQ: new REQ-034 (session history preservation)","files":null}]}